    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0538" n="442" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg442"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Governor Foster to
                        Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baton Rouge, La.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegram making further inquiry concerning the Tallulah lynching received. I
                    have wired the authorities of Madison Parish <pb facs="0539" n="443"
                        xml:id="pg443"/> requesting full history and information concerning the case
                    and what is being done by the local authorities. I will forward reply and
                    information as soon as it can be obtained.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Murphy J. Foster.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
